      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-484",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\theta -\\sin^2\\theta=\\cos 2\\theta.\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta = 3x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x = \\cos 6x,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t{\\int} \\left(\\cos^2 3x - \\sin^2 3x\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int  \\cos 6x\\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{1}{6}\\sin6x+ C.\\\n                                                                \n\t}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
